## Diagram Description

This class diagram illustrates the **Strategy pattern** applied to embedding model selection in the Python sidecar.

**Key design decisions**:

1. **Abstract base class (`BaseEmbeddingModel`)** — Defines the contract: `encode_image(image) → np.ndarray`. All concrete models implement lazy loading (`_load()`) and L2 normalization.
2. **Class attributes for metadata** — `model_name` and `vector_dim` are class-level constants, enabling the registry to inspect models without instantiating them.
3. **Lazy loading** — Models are loaded on first use (`_ensure_loaded()`), not at import time. This keeps sidecar startup fast and avoids loading 4 large models into memory simultaneously.
4. **Singleton cache (`_loaded_models`)** — Once a model is loaded, it is cached process-wide. Switching models requires a sidecar restart (acceptable for the evaluation protocol in §11.5).
5. **Registry pattern (`MODEL_REGISTRY`)** — Maps string identifiers to model classes. This enables runtime selection via env var or query parameter without conditional chains.

**Comparative dimensions**:

| Model | Library | Vector Dim | Pretraining | Hypothesized Strength |
|-------|---------|-----------|-------------|----------------------|
| Fashion-CLIP | open_clip | 512 | LAION-400M + fashion | Highest mAP (H1) |
| ResNet-50 | torchvision | 2048 | ImageNet-1K | Baseline CNN |
| EfficientNet-B0 | timm | 1280 | ImageNet-1K (AutoML) | Best mAP/ms (H2) |
| CLIP-generic | transformers | 512 | OpenAI WIT-400M | Semantic > visual (H4) |

**Evidence**: `service/Embedding/src/infra/models/base.py`, `service/Embedding/src/infra/models/fashion_clip.py`, `service/Embedding/src/infra/models/resnet_model.py`, `service/Embedding/src/infra/models/efficientnet_model.py`, `service/Embedding/src/infra/models/clip.py`, `service/Embedding/src/services/embedding_service.py`
